ic — bold color, strong portraiture, and a willingness to be loud in a way a lot of other genres aren't. But \\\"distinct\\\" doesn't hold if everyone converges on the same handful of moves. Here's where the visual language is actually heading in 2026.\"]}],[\"$\",\"hr\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"my-8 border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/30\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase text-[var(--paper)] mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/20\",\"children\":\"What's Been Working\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"A few approaches have proven durable rather than trendy:\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Strong central portraiture\"}],\" — a confident, well-lit portrait of the artist remains one of the most reliable formats, especially for singles and EPs where a face carries recognition\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Saturated, warm color grading\"}],\" — deep oranges, golds, and rich contrast continue to read as genre-appropriate and stand out in a streaming grid\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Typography as a design element, not an afterthought\"}],\" — artist name and title integrated into the composition rather than dropped on top as a label\"]}],\"$L5\",\"$L6\",\"$L7\",\"$L8\",\"$L9\",\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\"]}],\"$L17\"]}]}],\"$L18\",\"$L19\"]}],[\"$L1a\"],\"$L1b\"]}],\"isPartial\":\"$@1c\",\"staleTime\":\"$1d\",\"varyParams\":null},{\"rsc\":\"$L1e\",\"isPartial\":\"$@1f\",\"staleTime\":\"$1d\",\"varyParams\":null},{\"rsc\":\"$L20\",\"isPartial\":\"$@21\",\"staleTime\":\"$1d\",\"varyParams\":\"$22\"},{\"rsc\":\"$L23\",\"isPartial\":\"$@24\",\"staleTime\":\"$1d\",\"varyParams\":\"$22\"},{\"rsc\":\"$L25\",\"isPartial\":\"$@26\",\"staleTime\":\"$1d\",\"varyParams\":null}],\"isUpgradeableISRFallback\":false,\"a\":\"$@27\",\"rootVaryParams\":null,\"needsRuntimeRequest\":\"$@28\"}\n29:I[87879,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/3ykrlu0oa3rkw.js\"],\"default\"]\n2a:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n2b:\"$Sreact.suspense\"\n2d:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"ViewportBoundary\"]\n2e:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"MetadataBoundary\"]\n2f:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"IconMark\"]\n30:I[39756,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"default\"]\n31:I[37457,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0h2qsuyze9ds1.js\"],\"default\"]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/chunks/2b2j6nos8u62l.css\",\"style\"]\n5:[\"$\",\"li\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Cultural texture\"}],\" — patterns, fabric, and location cues used deliberately rather than decoratively, tying the visual to something specific rather than generic \\\"Afrocentric\\\" imagery\"]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase text-[var(--paper)] mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/20\",\"children\":\"What's Starting to Blend In\"}]\n7:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"The flip side: a few looks have become common enough that they're losing their impact.\"]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"li\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Generic gradient backgrounds\"}],\" with a cutout portrait — fast to produce, increasingly indistinguishable from a template\"]}]\n9:[\"$\",\"li\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Overly literal AI-generated compositions\"}],\" — technically polished but visually converging with thousands of similar outputs, which undercuts the \\\"stops the scroll\\\" job a cover is supposed to do\"]}]\na:[\"$\",\"li\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"ml-6 list-disc mb-2 text-[var(--paper-2)] font-sans\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Text-heavy covers with weak hierarchy\"}],\" — too many competing text elements fighting for attention on a thumbnail-sized image\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase text-[var(--paper)] mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/20\",\"children\":\"Where the Space Is Heading\"}]\nc:[\"$\",\"p\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"A few directions are gaining ground going into 2026:\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Illustration and stylized art over straight photography.\"}],\" More Afrobeats and alté-adjacent releases are leaning into illustrated or painterly covers rather than photo-based ones — closer to the visual language manga and graphic novel covers have used for years. It reads as more intentional and holds up better as a distinct visual identity across a body of work.\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Series consistency across a discography.\"}],\" Artists building a visual identity across multiple singles and an eventual project, rather than treating each cover as a one-off. This is where illustration has a real edge over photography or AI generation — a human illustrator can carry a consistent character, palette, or motif deliberately across releases.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"29\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"\",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"font-bold text-[var(--paper)]\",\"children\":\"Cross-genre visual borrowing.\"}],\" Manga-influenced linework, western graphic-novel coloring, and anime-adjacent character design are showing up more in Afrobeats and Nigerian hip-hop cover art — a genuinely distinct look in a genre where photographic portraiture has been the default for years.\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"hr\",\"31\",{\"className\":\"my-8 border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/30\"}]\n11:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"33\",{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase text-[var(--paper)] mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/20\",\"children\":\"What This Means If You're Releasing Music\"}]\n12:[\"$\",\"p\",\"35\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"If your goal is a cover that actually stands out on a crowded release day, the safest trend to follow isn't a specific color palette or pose — it's specificity. A cover built around your actual sound, story, and visual identity will outlast whatever the current dominant look is, because it isn't trying to look like everything else in the grid.\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"37\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"Illustrators working across album covers and manga-influenced styles — like \",[\"$\",\"a\",\"1\",{\"href\":\"/#order\",\"className\":\"text-[var(--yellow)] font-bold underline hover:text-[var(--red)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"commission work here\"}],\" — are increasingly the ones producing the covers that read as distinct rather than templated, precisely because the process is built around a specific brief rather than a fast, generic output.\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"hr\",\"39\",{\"className\":\"my-8 border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/30\"}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"41\",{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase text-[var(--paper)] mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--paper-2)]/20\",\"children\":\"Final Thoughts\"}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"43\",{\"className\":\"mb-4 font-sans leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"Afrobeats cover art is in an interesting moment — genuinely creative work sitting right next to a growing wave of fast, generic output. The covers that will still look good in two years are the ones built around a specific idea, not the ones chasing whatever's fastest to produce right now.\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-16 p-8 bg-[var(--paper)] text-[var(--ink)] border-2 border-[var(--ink)] shadow-[10px_10px_0_var(--red)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-xs text-[var(--red)] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1\",\"children\":\"Ready to Commission?\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-anton text-3xl uppercase mb-3\",\"children\":\"Get Your Custom Artwork Stamped\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-sans text-[var(--muted)] mb-6\",\"children\":\"Jhay Sanyay Studio handles custom cover art, manga/comic illustrations, and logo design from brief submission to final delivery. Fill out your job ticket below for a 48-hour quote.\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#order\",\"className\":\"stamp-btn inline-block !py-3 !px-6\",\"children\":\"FILL OUT JOB TICKET\"}]]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"$L29\",null,{}]\n19:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-[var(--ink)] border-t-2 border-[var(--paper-2)] py-10 color-[var(--paper-2)]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"wrap fl